CPython's list sort (runtime.c)
-------------------------------

The list sort in runtime.c (the section that starts with "list.sort is CPython 3.13's
timsort") is a port of the sort in CPython 3.13's Objects/listobject.c, designed in
Objects/listsort.txt. It is a derivative work of Python and is used under the Python
Software Foundation License Version 2, reproduced below.

Copyright (c) 2001-2024 Python Software Foundation; All Rights Reserved

Summary of the changes made to Python (clause 3 of the license): the lib/ modules are not
changed. The functions of the sort
(binarysort, count_run, gallop_left/gallop_right, merge_lo/merge_hi, merge_at, the
powersort run stack) are translated from C over PyObject pointers to C over Pystachy's
8-byte list slots. Comparisons go through Pystachy's type descriptors (or call back into the
compiled program's __lt__ methods) instead of PyObject_RichCompare, in the same order as
CPython makes them; key= and the type-specialized compare functions are left out; ints and
floats are merged with branch-free selects; and the merge buffer is memory that Pystachy's
garbage collector scans.

